1001
01:31:51.561 --> 01:31:56.847
Before we begin, bring a concise picture
of your students back into view. Include

1002
01:31:56.848 --> 01:32:02.134
their strengths, interests and sources of
joy. Think about communication, sensory

1003
01:32:02.135 --> 01:32:07.223
experience and thinking; what costs and
what lightens; identity and belonging.

1004
01:32:07.224 --> 01:32:11.916
Include what students, families and the
team already know, alongside the

1005
01:32:11.917 --> 01:32:16.872
questions still open. These are prompts to
hold in mind, not another form to

1006
01:32:16.873 --> 01:32:22.093
complete. We’re not building a file on one
child, and we’re not ranking students

1007
01:32:22.094 --> 01:32:27.116
by need. We’re keeping real, different
people in view as we design. Later, in

1008
01:32:27.117 --> 01:32:32.271
the private check, you’ll return to each
